#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0270 expect=violation domain=TS
#note "Boundary for the leaf parameter 'negative: false': a negative duration '-P80Y' is not an acceptable planned maximum age, so it must be flagged. With the default (negative omitted / true) the leading minus would be accepted and this scenario would go green. No class= (the twins declare none and Scope carries no Classes axis). ADAPTED-FROM fda/FDA-SD1215/FDA-SD1215-invalid_negative-TS.cdt."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 TSPARMCD=AGEMAX TSVAL=-P80Y
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | 1 | AGEMAX | Planned Maximum Age of Subjects | -P80Y
